DESCRIPTION:Occidental Vitality Sessions: Nutrition\, Metabolism\, & the A
 rt of Living Well\n2026–2027 Monthly Nutrition & Wellness Series\nExplor
 ing nutrition\, metabolism\, and the everyday habits that help us thrive. 
 Monthly classes with Mary Sheila Gonnella\, BCHN\, Holistic Nutritionist &
  Ayurvedic Educator Second Wednesdays in the OCA Studio\n$20/session or $1
 5 for OCA members\nPresented by:\nMary Sheila Gonnella\, BCHN\, NC\, Ayurv
 edic Educator of Occidental Nutrition\nWednesday\, December 9: The Food-Mo
 od Connection for Nervous System Health\nYour nervous system influences ho
 w you feel\, think\, digest\, sleep and respond to everyday stress. Discov
 er how nutrition\, blood sugar balance\, and the gut-brain connection infl
 uence your mood and emotional well-being\, immunity\, and overall health. 
 We’ll explore nourishing foods\, mindful eating\, and simple daily pract
 ices that help support a calmer\, more resilient nervous system.\nRegister
 \n2026-2027 Schedule:\nNov 11: Immune Resilience Through The Decades\nDec 
 9: The Food-Mood Connection for Nervous System Health\nJan 13: Supporting 
 Your Changing Metabolism\nFeb 10: Blood Sugar Secrets: More Energy\, Fewer
  Cravings\nMarch 10: The Energy Equation: Thyroid Health\, Stress & Metabo
 lism\nApril 14: The Protein & Fiber Longevity Connection\nMay 12: Strong B
 ones\, Strong Body\nJune 9: The Anti-Inflammatory Kitchen\nJuly 14: Digest
 ive Health Essentials: Beyond Probiotics\nAug 11: Brain Power: Food\, Mood
  & Memory\nSept 8: Hormone Harmony: Understanding Your Changing Body\nOct 
 13: The Secrets to Better Sleep: Restore Your Natural Rhythms\nNov 10: Lov
 e Your Heart: Beyond Cholesterol\nDec 8: Seasonal Wisdom for Winter Wellne
 ss
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3820 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, United States
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/occidental-
 vitality-session-sn768
